    {
      "id": "otel-deep-research",
      "type": "research",
      "label": "Deep research: local-OTEL + git-refs",
      "status": "done",
      "next": [
        "plan"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-06-27T00:47:54.760Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-06-27T02:08:08.334Z",
      "branch_of": "plan",
      "note": "Perplexity x2: (A) OTLP-as-files is a staging format not archival — pin schema_url, one-file-per-signal, cumulative-per-session, collector-as-checker guards silent drops; (B) git-refs is the 'too many refs' anti-pattern — keep-and-harden at low volume or migrate to git-notes/object-storage. Feeds 2 workshops.",
      "artifacts": [
        "docs/plans/038-telemetry-otel-standard/research-storage-and-transport.md"
      ],
      "comments": [
        {
          "at": "2026-06-27T02:08:08.334Z",
          "text": "Pass 2 (transport): git-notes REJECTED as migration target — single notes-ref reintroduces NFF write-contention + orphan-commit object bloat (lateral-to-worse vs embarrassingly-parallel one-ref-per-session). No real tool uses git transport; end-state is store-and-forward (spool→uploader→OTEL Collector / object-storage). Live fork = keep-and-harden-now vs leave-git, with a graduation tripwire.",
          "kind": "decision"
        }
      ]
    },
